package cajeta.gpu.core;

/**
 * AsImpl — an app's preference for how an {@link AccelerationStructure} is built:
 * the portable software BVH or the device's native acceleration structure. Passed
 * to {@link AccelerationStructure#of}; the default constructor uses {@link #Auto}.
 *
 * This is the model's **capability heuristic with explicit override**
 * (cajeta-docs/gpu/CajetaGPU.md §1.5): `Auto` takes the hardware fast path when
 * the active device advertises native inline ray query (see {@link Device#supports})
 * and the portable software floor otherwise; `Software` / `Native` force the choice.
 * Hardware ray tracing can LOSE to a software BVH at large query radius / extreme
 * density, so an app that knows its query pattern can force `Software` even on a
 * ray-query-capable GPU — and the verb follows the noun (the kernel runs the
 * software BVH walk).
 *
 *     // auto (native if the device has it, else software):
 *     AccelerationStructure scene = heap AccelerationStructure(boxes, n);
 *     // force the software BVH on whatever device is active:
 *     AccelerationStructure soft = AccelerationStructure.of(boxes, n, AsImpl.Software);
 *
 * A global `CAJETA_GPU_AS_IMPL=software|native` environment variable overrides this
 * per process (env wins), mirroring `CAJETA_XPU_BACKEND`.
 *
 * DROP THE SOFTWARE FLOOR (`NativeNoFloor`). On CUDA the multi-impl model normally
 * keeps the portable software BVH as a FLOOR alongside the native (OptiX) rep, so an
 * Unsupported-shape kernel can fall back to it instead of faulting. `NativeNoFloor` is
 * the caller's assertion that EVERY consuming kernel is a supported native shape, so the
 * floor is omitted — trading the safety net for the memory + build time of the second
 * representation. If a kernel that cannot traverse the native rep is then launched, the
 * runtime diagnoses and skips that launch (it never reads the native handle as a BVH
 * blob). Behaves exactly like `Native` where there is no separate floor to drop (Vulkan
 * native, or any device that falls back to the software BVH as its only rep).
 *
 *     // OptiX RT cores only, no software floor (all consumers are supported shapes):
 *     AccelerationStructure rt = AccelerationStructure.of(boxes, n, AsImpl.NativeNoFloor);
 *
 * The ordinal is the **stable native contract** — it MUST match `CajetaAsPref` in
 * runtime/native/cajeta_noun_impl.h (the runtime resolver switches on it). Do not
 * reorder; append only.
 */
public enum AsImpl {
    Auto,           // 0 — heuristic default (native if supported, else software)
    Software,       // 1 — force the portable software BVH
    Native,         // 2 — prefer native (falls back to software if unsupported)
    NativeNoFloor   // 3 — prefer native AND drop the software floor (all consumers
                    //     are supported native shapes; trades the fallback for memory)
}
